            'For many football fans in Nigeria and across Africa, mobile data is a real cost, and a long match can use a lot of it. Live scores do not need much data if you use them carefully. This guide explains how to follow football without wasting bundles.',
            '## Why scores use less data than video',
            'Watching a match on a stream can use hundreds of megabytes in an hour. A live-score page uses only a tiny amount of data each time it updates, so following the score instead of the video can use far less data. If you cannot watch the match, a live-score page and goal alerts give you almost everything that matters.',
